📅 Week 8 – Project Setup

Commit: Set up development environment and project structure for Smart Finance Assistant

This commit established the foundation of the project by configuring the development environment and installing required 
dependencies. Initial setup issues related to missing packages and version mismatches were resolved during this stage. 
This ensured the system was ready for further development and AI integration.

📅 Week 9 – Data Processing Pipeline

Commit: Implement data cleaning and preprocessing pipeline for financial transactions

This commit introduced a structured data processing system for handling financial CSV files. Currency symbols were
cleaned, missing values were managed, and transaction data was properly formatted using pandas. This step was
essential to ensure accurate financial analysis.

📅 Week 10 – AI Integration & Chatbot Development

Commit: Integrate chatbot functionality and implement RAG-based financial assistant system

This commit focused on integrating AI-driven chatbot functionality. A retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) system
was implemented to allow the assistant to respond using real transaction data. Early versions were refined to 
improve contextual accuracy and reduce generic responses.

📅 Week 11 – Tool Development & Automation

Commit: Develop savings calculator tool for financial planning automation

This commit introduced a savings projection tool that calculates progress toward financial goals. AI assistance was
used to design and refine formulas into reusable functions. Input validation was also improved to handle incorrect 
or missing user inputs.

📅 Week 12 – Testing & System Validation

Commit: Develop test suite for validating Smart Finance Assistant functionality

This final commit focused on testing and debugging the system. A structured test suite was created to evaluate core
functions, including edge cases and invalid inputs. Several issues were identified and fixed, improving overall 
system reliability and robustness.





